{"caller": "codex", "commit": "e27032797dffd1495e99d98a147ff5a022d4727d", "date": "2026-10-06T09:13:45+00:00", "exit": 1, "files": ["BundleChecker.lean", "ProofChecker.lean", "README.md", "build-support/README.md", "build-support/lean-toolchain.nix", "build-support/lean4export-skip-trusted.patch", "build-support/lean4export.nix", "docs/data-path.md", "docs/execution-profile.md", "docs/install.md", "docs/kernel-gate.md", "lean-toolchain", "migration_check/runtime.py", "plans/20261006-lean-4-34-1-upgrade.status.md", "reports/20261006-lean-4341-upgrade-darwin.json", "reviews/log.jsonl"], "findings": [{"id": "20261006T091345Z-e2703279#1", "line": 115, "path": "BundleChecker.lean", "rule": "R8", "severity": "must", "text": "The bundle checker's replay chain (`schemaEnvironment` and `checkBundle`, lines 115 and 124-129) now goes through `Environment.toKernelEnv.replay` and `Environment.ofKernelEnv`, which changes how the kernel gate builds the trusted and checked environments; owner review required. Fix: have the owner confirm that the kernel replay API in Lean 4.34.1 gives the same checks as the removed `Environment.replay`, including the axiom audit and target comparison on the result of `ofKernelEnv`."}, {"id": "20261006T091345Z-e2703279#2", "line": 20, "path": "ProofChecker.lean", "rule": "R8", "severity": "must", "text": "The proof checker's three replay steps (lines 20, 22 and 25) now use `toKernelEnv.replay` and `Environment.ofKernelEnv` in the kernel gate; owner review required. Fix: have the owner confirm that the replayed environment passed to `checkTarget` still holds all declarations replayed by the kernel."}, {"id": "20261006T091345Z-e2703279#3", "line": 8, "path": "build-support/lean4export.nix", "rule": "R8", "severity": "must", "text": "The export path now uses lean4export v4.34.0 (`076e8e57…`). Its upstream `dumpConstant` also skips `partial` declarations unless unsafe export is on (see the patch context at `build-support/lean4export-skip-trusted.patch:23`); owner review required. Fix: have the owner review the new exporter pin and the changed skip condition before the bundle path is accepted."}, {"id": "20261006T091345Z-e2703279#4", "line": 51, "path": "migration_check/runtime.py", "rule": "R10", "severity": "should", "text": "The changed message \"The verifier requires the pinned Lean 4.34.1 runtime\" does not name the Lean version that was found, or its sysroot, and does not say what the user can do next. Fix: include the detected version and sysroot, and tell the user to set `MIGRATION_CHECK_LEAN_SYSROOT` to a Lean 4.34.1 installation or to reinstall the verifier."}, {"id": "20261006T091345Z-e2703279#5", "line": 50, "path": "migration_check/runtime.py", "rule": "R1", "severity": "should", "text": "The pinned Lean version is a string literal inside the `locate` check, and the error message on the next line repeats it, so this commit had to edit the pin in two places. Fix: define a named constant such as `PINNED_LEAN_VERSION` with a docstring, and use it in both the check and the message."}], "id": "20261006T091345Z-e2703279", "kind": "review", "reviewer": "claude", "revision": "@-", "rules": {"R1": "62d446279093", "R10": "638d8cbd1df8", "R11": "5de19cdbbbc1", "R12": "99f66579f467", "R13": "da0926dafb88", "R2": "e5e78fb2a52a", "R3": "4f9188eadd60", "R4": "ea7ca17539eb", "R5": "b8613a2d693b", "R6": "5600dce59aef", "R7": "0b68df581c57", "R8": "b4168359c60d", "R9": "5a69196344d0"}, "well_formed": true}
